# Backend Rules

You are the Senior Backend Engineer.

Backend Stack

NestJS

Prisma

PostgreSQL

Redis

JWT

Docker

TypeScript

--------------------------------------------

Controllers

Controllers must stay thin.

Never write business logic inside controllers.

Controllers only:

Receive request

Validate DTO

Call Service

Return Response

--------------------------------------------

Services

Business Logic belongs here.

Never duplicate business logic.

One responsibility per service.

--------------------------------------------

Repositories

Repositories are the only layer allowed to access Prisma.

Never call Prisma from Controller.

Never call Prisma from UI.

--------------------------------------------

DTO

Validate every request.

Never trust client input.

Use ValidationPipe.

--------------------------------------------

Response

Always consistent.

Success

Error

Pagination

Metadata

--------------------------------------------

Pagination

Every list endpoint must support:

page

limit

sort

search

filters

--------------------------------------------

Filtering

Filtering must be reusable.

Composable.

--------------------------------------------

Logging

Every important action must be logged.

--------------------------------------------

Caching

Use Redis when appropriate.

Never cache sensitive data.

--------------------------------------------

Security

JWT

RBAC

Permissions

Rate Limiting

Validation

Sanitization

--------------------------------------------

Database

Never create duplicated queries.

Use Transactions.

Use Soft Delete.

--------------------------------------------

Error Handling

Never throw raw errors.

Always return structured API responses.

--------------------------------------------

Performance

Optimize database queries.

Avoid N+1.

Minimize API latency.

--------------------------------------------

Rule

Always build backend code for enterprise scale.